  "notes": "DM3-D is the Dante-equipped variant of the DM3 22-channel digital mixer; it adds two etherCON Dante ports (PRIMARY/SECONDARY) versus the base DM3, which is otherwise identical in I/O. Of the 16 Mic/Line inputs, 12 are XLR-only and 4 are XLR/TRS combo jacks (modeled as 12 separate XLR-only ports + 4 combo XLR-primary/TRS-accepts ports). Power is supplied via an external DC power supply (Yamaha PA-L500, 24V/2.5A) through a locking 4-pin XLR DC connector, not an internal PSU/IEC inlet. Desktop console form factor, not rack-mountable, so rackUnits omitted. Grades omitted for Ethernet/Dante and USB ports because Yamaha's spec sheet does not state a link-speed/USB generation beyond \"USB2.0\" for USB TO HOST (included as usb-2.0) and does not specify Dante/Network link speed (typically 100Mb/1Gb Dante over standard Ethernet, but not stated on spec page, so omitted rather than guessed for those ports).",
